so what is top down communication and if  you read all the books and articles  about that you will find out that there  are lots of definitions many people  claiming different things to be down  communication so I really want to  simplify it for you so in my experience  what this really comes down to is two  things namely first in your  communication to focus on the results to  focus on the content to only focus on  the things that really matter to your  audience and second always starting your  communication with the key message with  the key result that you want to  communicate to your audience and the  main error that many people do is not  starting with this result with this key  message but rather starting with all the  individual details with all the little  arguments that when your whole case is  composed of and then only in the very  end to then draw the conclusion from it  so they pretty much turn the pyramid  around and this for many different  reasons is not considered effective  communication
 

